## The one invariant this bridge preserves

Every admitted capability is a `sosa:Procedure` classified `Read`
(sosa:Observation-shaped) or `Do` (sosa:Actuation-shaped) via
`dct:type` — enforced at sync time by GymAct's own real SHACL shape
(`urn:gymact:shape:capability`, wired via this pack's `shape:` template
frontmatter), not a bridge-invented constraint. A capability whose
`dct:type` falls outside the admitted
`{urn:gymact:consequence:read, urn:gymact:consequence:do}` set is refused
by that real shape before any output is written — the same fail-closed
rule GymAct enforces on its own capability data, and the same rule
